      "typical_award_size": "HACM owns 244 public housing units in the City of Madera, operates the Pomona Ranch Housing Center and USDA farm labor housing, and administers about 800 Housing Choice Vouchers countywide (small, qualified PHA). The FY 2026-27 Agency Plan (public notice May 2026, drafts June 2026) lists as goals evaluating project-based voucher initiatives, pursuing affordable housing development partnerships, tax credit and mixed-finance opportunities, Faircloth authority and RAD or Section 18 conversion of public housing; Attachment 2 states HACM is exploring project-basing vouchers in opportunity zones as opportunities arise. No PBVs are currently awarded and no RFP has been issued.",
